# Feature documentation required

**No feature ships without documentation.** When adding or materially updating a capability, update docs in the **same session** (same commit / PR batch) — not as a follow-up.

## Minimum updates by change type

| Change | Document |
|--------|----------|
| New command, API route, UI flow, Discord behavior | README + CHANGELOG + ARCHITECTURE (and `docs/reference/` if a stable contract) |
| Changed behavior users or ops will notice | CHANGELOG + update affected living docs |
| New or renamed env / config keys | `config.env.example` or `.env.example` + ARCHITECTURE § env |
| New integration or reaction map | Reference spec + README summary |

## Gate before commit / push / deploy

Do **not** commit, push, or ask Jason to deploy until:

- [ ] CHANGELOG (or `docs/CHANGELOG.md`) has prepend-only bullets for the work
- [ ] At least one durable doc beyond code comments describes the feature (README, ARCHITECTURE, PRD, API, RUNBOOK, or `docs/reference/`)
- [ ] CURSOR.md updated if commands, deploy state, or handover changed
- [ ] Config templates updated if env contract changed

## Where to look (by org)

| Org | Canonical standards |
|-----|---------------------|
| **Yingson Labs** | `lab-standards/docs/documentation-standards.md` § Feature documentation |
| **WavePoint** | `docs/documentation-standards.md` § Feature documentation |

If unsure which files to touch, read the repo’s `docs/documentation-standards.md` agent checklist and `docs/README.md` index (if present).
